#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114987 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "dc6dd9b4-de7f-52d0-8ff9-a7a7f7a9abd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4711" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/a50d551e5d8abe8d9ae48778b195c382bbbf96f6fc5083c41b67642e99deffda.png)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/48c423256fbdc0d7e4f6ff716fb449efe6f98bdf57ba90353bcced930ea4ed17.png)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/81b7626ac30b06c5eeb10be274dd93476a86dce5fe3053722d96e16b78d7f165.png)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-5y \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114988 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/id #uuid "f2c7cfd3-da43-5208-bd0e-21692357fabe" :question/math-academy-id "e-4712" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y=1, \\\\ 4x+ky=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/f4478e5828da7c79a47bf3ca212ed15357befe7b0b208c78beb0895b445272c9.png)\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/cfea36ae2b5cb5d8715480c1e0ee0b5ba06cf39d0c2032eb6e9b9078bf8c5bde.png)\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115041 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/id #uuid "cd56314d-f45a-55be-9762-983fe507a1a0" :question/math-academy-id "e-6173" :question/problem "Given the system\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/427c19efbebba6bfe2dc36bccd852d7a1f5e0ec97dc46c00043d019807e86ec2.png)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/50f13deaa03c2af30f511ef3d514e3dd2e118d81d9b121b436ff1a2f2497c303.png)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/e02bb5004f792eea20216e64098bb924dbed15defb9330967d6ae5a144e067dc.png)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d7bbd4-4dcd-5f2c-a52d-4451d28a9855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385569} {:answer/id #uuid "909c2fa2-18bb-56f6-a07f-ffbd60e70395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 1-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385570} {:answer/id #uuid "8230423a-b173-5e28-a487-08578c77c8ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385571} {:answer/id #uuid "78e22ea5-4a2a-5074-807e-b38670f29eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385572} {:answer/id #uuid "e44c7a57-9f6f-57ab-a0d0-44cc92029548" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 1-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78e22ea5-4a2a-5074-807e-b38670f29eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385572} :answer-field/id #uuid "917e81fc-fd40-5388-84ae-8fd66738e6b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f67dc1c-a8f3-5dc9-a4b3-b289bc053549" :question/math-academy-id "q-131715" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=1 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f81946b8-0e51-5d2c-a843-bc2231e1d145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317567} {:answer/id #uuid "4e841753-e6ff-5ea7-b26f-6d9575329fa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317568} {:answer/id #uuid "33e69ce1-6954-5201-8c9c-5e864e29e461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317569} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3ae4ee-b56e-5f4e-aae8-59dacc65408d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317570} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ba308b-dbba-56f5-baa5-466e5aeb13fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5ba308b-dbba-56f5-baa5-466e5aeb13fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317571} :answer-field/id #uuid "33fce12e-12f7-5945-a801-72dea6bcf2e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85139672-fc12-5f19-974e-cd9c9c3f59d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-131719" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=-1 \\\\  & 2x+8y=-2 \\\\  & -3x-12y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8903f11-0cba-58d2-be49-cac41448500a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385576} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4b9a6b-af1a-5623-a24c-5b1ad6705419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385577} {:answer/id #uuid "4339f9f5-91ec-5c96-8cf9-fc8bdef769b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385578} {:answer/id #uuid "7fcb2f4a-73fa-58f0-a9e0-167d0c8521ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385579} {:answer/id #uuid "a2223ece-52c7-5aa8-9edb-669f38312dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb4b9a6b-af1a-5623-a24c-5b1ad6705419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385577} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c6ce4e-208b-5270-84b0-c69fca8d4c92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0683e131-d27c-52ac-9ea2-e2395865251d" :question/math-academy-id "q-131723" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+z=3 \\\\  & -3x+3y-3z=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=19,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c13a8f7e-82f0-53ac-9688-c35a2cf68ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385583} {:answer/id #uuid "6f410d1e-ecab-5375-beb3-384d5f377665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385584} {:answer/id #uuid "a5853016-6db8-5d71-b85b-ba03606577be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385585} {:answer/id #uuid "91bc9db8-f764-53dc-b349-1b457d68b0c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385586} {:answer/id #uuid "5db4c8bd-c840-5d2f-92ae-f598d638c7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91bc9db8-f764-53dc-b349-1b457d68b0c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385586} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a82629-076c-55ed-87f4-03609f626ead" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc0a4fe5-74aa-50e7-beb1-354fa029945a" :question/math-academy-id "q-131728" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -x+4y=-2 \\\\  & -3x+(3k+15)y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 3k+15 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 3k+15 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3k+3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x+4y=-2 \\\\ (3k+3)y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-1,$ then the second equation is $0=2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c7cf958-a6d8-5621-ae52-1c50f6662bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113427} {:answer/id #uuid "a07f08f3-f487-508d-b37a-4482389df0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113428} {:answer/id #uuid "a3eaf318-39b0-508d-8361-519d5b17b7dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113429} {:answer/id #uuid "f1bff38a-e2eb-5637-8051-86af4e274548" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113430} {:answer/id #uuid "4dcfd229-b4a1-5190-bc65-819b917d55dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dcfd229-b4a1-5190-bc65-819b917d55dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113431} :answer-field/id #uuid "1efc6a3d-dcbe-51a0-8f3b-826fd8a5a662" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "402ab26a-a0df-5fc5-a264-b91a4c6d7d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-32242" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -x+2y=6 \\\\  & 2x-3y=13 \\\\  & 5x-y=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system has a unique solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 75\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -150\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-150,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bab7fe73-70ab-5b84-9739-004c2f2afa8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385590} {:answer/id #uuid "50e513f9-1edf-5458-abba-862ad8fef510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385591} {:answer/id #uuid "d118b054-3fca-57cc-9d35-5c8c6f1781ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385592} {:answer/id #uuid "b45c8970-e537-5630-8f61-c34fc7981c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385593} {:answer/id #uuid "dce17f1d-c0aa-5913-b539-da9dc55dabe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bab7fe73-70ab-5b84-9739-004c2f2afa8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385590} :answer-field/id #uuid "590002f2-d7a2-5ecd-9881-510b1a3b5477" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "376102dd-bbbf-5006-9d2c-7f1bfeb57afa" :question/math-academy-id "q-32245" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=3 \\\\  & 4x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & k & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & k & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & k+2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=3 \\\\  & (k+2)y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nNow if $k=-2$, then the second equation is $0=-2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when  $k=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115672 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99166388-f058-5f72-b80c-5b4282a522cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113433} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e9df98-67f7-54c0-8ec3-bce6cc775993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = \\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113434} {:answer/id #uuid "f60f9877-fd36-59d9-a3ec-527b98368e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113435} {:answer/id #uuid "284ec6b1-1f86-5100-be3a-3e470bb91463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k =-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113436} {:answer/id #uuid "404830dc-4c84-5f9f-b429-3660dc356338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k =-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f60f9877-fd36-59d9-a3ec-527b98368e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113435} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f40e7bb-c091-5bfa-b08f-acb863997d65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a9a3feb-6c16-50e8-885d-ee5cd242ab95" :question/math-academy-id "q-32246" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+4y=12 \\\\  & x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4-3k & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+ky=4 \\\\  & (4-3k)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=\\frac{4}{3},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=4.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=\\frac{4}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "967daa91-b36c-5199-a6dd-973438d43f0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385597} {:answer/id #uuid "aa505b02-67fd-5c1a-a4b1-f43919215056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8-{x}_{3} \\\\ 3+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385598} {:answer/id #uuid "0941ed57-66f2-5bfa-a959-791260e8b78e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8-8{x}_{3} \\\\ 6-6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385599} {:answer/id #uuid "dd01a611-cf5a-52f4-8671-8c5924b96a1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8-6{x}_{3} \\\\ 10+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385600} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf599c5-1f89-5564-83e8-c699531c8005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8-{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "967daa91-b36c-5199-a6dd-973438d43f0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385597} :answer-field/id #uuid "19546a12-a85b-5327-a3e4-e7420e808b8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f65d67ed-b94b-50cc-87d4-9aa7130f7547" :question/math-academy-id "q-32247" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 10 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+10{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}=6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7350dcb-841e-5c20-90e7-b93a5bf3bd18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385604} {:answer/id #uuid "cb05ac8b-114a-5b89-b8cd-4ce7f6db1a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385605} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab3d6ce-f83d-565f-851a-dee93be4b534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385606} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5c11c8-ee19-52d5-8def-53d2afc159e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385607} {:answer/id #uuid "63541c9d-3721-507f-97f8-7b3580959b14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e5c11c8-ee19-52d5-8def-53d2afc159e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385607} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ece34b0-c76f-55e4-9de2-dd23f3634491" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1591cfc-e875-5fb0-8595-3680a837d9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-32331" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4x-y=2 \\\\ 8x+ky=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & k & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & k & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-2 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4x-y=2 \\\\ (k-2)y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=2,$ then the second equation is $0=9,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385609 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b78a38-327a-5e55-8803-4594cf93a041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385611} {:answer/id #uuid "323a9d22-0906-5ac6-b26b-a217e22bd2ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 6+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385612} {:answer/id #uuid "9ed78420-edf3-58ec-9c71-ee29ab0a285d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385613} {:answer/id #uuid "6e613a85-d888-5eb4-a954-af032f56232d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 6-2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385614} {:answer/id #uuid "cab7c415-c70e-5f9f-9729-8c2e85df7992" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b78a38-327a-5e55-8803-4594cf93a041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385611} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7b39adf-fa97-586f-a4b5-56acfdfb11ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385610}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1276fcd-8439-5e1a-b9b9-d1caf9143cd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-32517" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now   \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ Since we have that ${x}_{1}=4$,  we only need to find ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-6-2{x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8fb9412-eb4b-5fc7-a668-6254be1176b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317616} {:answer/id #uuid "180aa355-38f3-5bc4-a98d-6089535eaac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317617} {:answer/id #uuid "43677cd0-73bf-5272-95a1-c7d210e1257c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-z \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317618} {:answer/id #uuid "3a715954-196e-5121-9eb2-a071e7214ff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317619} {:answer/id #uuid "118b2c2b-be06-5fce-b85e-7beb4cab4232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a715954-196e-5121-9eb2-a071e7214ff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317619} :answer-field/id #uuid "47bbcdd9-b23e-52e8-94f0-96d651969d9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "013e11bb-39c0-595b-a244-03847638286f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42019" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+2z=2 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=0 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ y=z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a74658ab-6621-565d-8a89-7358301574eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2+4z \\\\ 1-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317630} {:answer/id #uuid "192b6da6-515a-5d39-94fe-459d8d85fff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317631} {:answer/id #uuid "d956ce98-8354-52ea-b7e2-6f47d9302574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2z \\\\ 4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317632} {:answer/id #uuid "289b5e1b-d5de-5cd8-a853-a1325eb3ba0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2+4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317633} {:answer/id #uuid "41109a43-3c87-59ca-bcc7-229b8a8eb449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+4z \\\\ 3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "192b6da6-515a-5d39-94fe-459d8d85fff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317631} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc7d8608-6cac-5579-9b7d-8a78b7ebbee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09fe1174-4802-515f-8d41-d02fb865fb55" :question/math-academy-id "q-42041" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-4z=2 \\\\ 4x+y-5z=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+2z \\\\ y=-3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad86b22-14be-5e9f-bff6-1f59bd821811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385618} {:answer/id #uuid "9bdd1799-cdc9-5139-aec4-20001e1cc368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385619} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d8ed49-54fa-511e-9a07-7ee04a050d33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385620} {:answer/id #uuid "6527d1f8-72a9-5494-8eb5-d08c6be2cfe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385621} {:answer/id #uuid "7b010199-eef9-594b-b6e1-42d90a7c9fb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0d8ed49-54fa-511e-9a07-7ee04a050d33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385620} :answer-field/id #uuid "87ebdf2e-af41-581e-bbaa-7bee509ba00e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8971116-e24d-5808-9b29-a50e168511e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74634" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=-1 \\\\  & 2x-4y=3 \\\\  & x+y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is inconsistent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we will first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=\\frac{9}{2},$ and it has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385623 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e639ba-4dbd-52bb-9394-d20de49599be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385625} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa6f2d7-7ddf-5ef0-8bd8-3d6520f6749a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385626} {:answer/id #uuid "038f9894-7ae9-54fc-8204-130733db04ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385627} {:answer/id #uuid "d10bc068-126f-5bf1-86c6-4c0fc9a9ac77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385628} {:answer/id #uuid "23ea33af-353a-587d-a585-3ce7253c8eaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "038f9894-7ae9-54fc-8204-130733db04ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385627} :answer-field/id #uuid "775db22b-f86c-52a4-90cd-ffb53454c701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5392e02e-d3ba-5c84-8504-8157a2d355a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-74635" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -2x+4y+3z=0 \\\\  & x+3y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & \\frac{3}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means that  we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aac4128b-fbb4-5f62-a427-6c635795c9ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385632} {:answer/id #uuid "975abafb-200d-5acd-b96d-43ff7f0955c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385633} {:answer/id #uuid "dacb82b0-435f-5982-a260-7e38dbf9a896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385634} {:answer/id #uuid "baa721f5-c7c3-552c-b8af-e4f89ee49386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385635} {:answer/id #uuid "ce7bb673-c499-59af-a1d4-f4b0c5832e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac4128b-fbb4-5f62-a427-6c635795c9ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385632} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9963516-60ab-574d-b90b-2fb7bfc137c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d104654a-9fe8-585c-a338-f036b730d697" :question/math-academy-id "q-74688" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-4 \\\\  & 3x+2ky=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2k & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2k & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2k-6 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-4 \\\\ (2k-6)y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=3,$ then the second equation is $0=10,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=3.$"}]}
